      "claim": "The artifact is classified as a review and its missing GIFT is justified on the basis that the page itself provides retrieval practice, but each graded shell, Git, and AI check is immediately preceded by an answer-bearing teaching step. This makes the three scored activities primarily immediate recognition after a refresher rather than an honest check of what the learner can retrieve; the learner-facing title also calls this formative page a course check even though the manifest calls it Practice: Foundations course review and the module distinguishes it from the platform assessment.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "url": "https://ies.ed.gov/ncee/wwc/Docs/PracticeGuide/20072004.pdf",
          "section": "Recommendation 5, especially 5a: require answers before introducing the topic; use quizzing with active retrieval",
